WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.600
There's no holiday quite like the Purge and
that's a good thing.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.460
But what if it were real, this one night out
of the year in which all crime, including

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:09.620
murder, was legal?

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.220
Would you hide, or would you seek?

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:17.300
The Purge scratches the same itch as a zombie
movie, imagining a lawless world where it's

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.340
kill or be killed.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.120
If the Purge really did pop off, would you
be prepared?

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.619
Over four stories of survival and anarchy,
we've noticed some strategies that would help

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:29.159
you survive, along with a few tactics to avoid
at all costs.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.780
Grab your notebook and pay attention to the
do's and don'ts of Purge night.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.900
Do: Prior preparation

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.700
Ask any manager type about the five Ps, and
they'll tell you: "Proper planning prevents

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.640
poor performance."

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.660
It's a principle that can be applied to everything
from food service to the front lines.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:48.970
So if the sirens go off and you haven't yet
built up a stockpile of useful goods, then

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:51.030
you deserve whatever's coming to you.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:55.480
Frank Grillo's character Leo Barnes demonstrates
the preparation principle perfectly.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:59.280
There's also The First Purge's Dmitri, who
prepared for purging by getting his hands

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.950
on every gun that's ever washed up on Staten
Island.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.030
So follow their examples.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:06.040
You should also probably learn some martial
arts.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.320
Don't: Cultivate grudges

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:13.330
Purge or no Purge, the key to not being killed
by your neighbors is to not give your neighbors

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:13.820
a reason.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.500
This can be accomplished by just being a considerate
person, and not giving people any cause to

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.070
think about your name when the ol' "murder
is legal" holiday comes around.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.560
Otherwise, you could end up like the Sandin
family, ringed in by resentful neighbors,

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.620
with targets on your back.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:31.160
Probably should've participated in the neighborhood
rummage sale, guys!

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.580
Do: The buddy system

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.530
Braving the Purge alone could be a one-way
ticket to the morgue.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:41.200
You never know when a marauding team of dirt
bikers, paramilitary goons, or the K might

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:41.820
be lurking.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.270
If you wanna survive, you need friends.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.229
The Purge: Anarchy is all about the value
of friendship in the trenches, with Sergeant

00:01:48.229 --> 00:01:52.800
Barnes going from a vengeance-driven lone
wolf to a righteous defender of the weak.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:56.800
In turn, the people he protects have his back,
and ultimately save his soul.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:01.360
The only person who makes the one-man-army
route work for him is The First Purge's Dmitri,

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:04.940
who goes full Rambo on a towerful of armed
invaders.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.280
But that only ends up being the case after
his entire team is assassinated via drone

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.600
strike, and not even he gets the job done
all by himself.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.800
Don't: Get cocky

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.200
Across all of the Purge movies, it's shocking
how many participants serve themselves up

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.540
as easy targets, twirling in the streets and
basically asking for a bullet.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:24.260
Don't let this be you!

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.560
Instead, up your chances of survival by staying
humble and praying for dawn.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.030
Don't get caught up in acts of pretentious
ritual murder, which backfire far too frequently.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:37.420
And don't be out in the road in a tank top
and a bunny mask, flexing and taunting people.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.780
That's how you get a crossbow bolt to the
chest from the real heroes.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.000
Murder's legal for everyone, remember?

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:44.900
Do: Armor up

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:49.510
Even mall cops wear bulletproof vests when
they go to work, so why do so many Purgers

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:53.300
dress like they're going to a warehouse rave
instead of an unhinged massacre?

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:57.420
Purgers put all their focus on the mask, when
they should really be hitting the streets

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.800
dressed like Robocop.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.600
They don't even wear helmets!

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.780
In that way, purging is like riding a bicycle.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.080
Are you trying to look cool, or do you want
to get home alive?

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:07.800
Don't: be obsessive

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:12.240
After going through each Purge movie with
a team of experts, we've determined that Purge

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.280
night is actually not a great time to settle
scores.

00:03:15.349 --> 00:03:19.240
Countless people die on some lonely hills
over the course of the films, just because

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:23.770
they couldn't let things go, from the candy-obsessed
girl in Election Year to the first movie's

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:27.160
squad of prep school creeps who couldn't let
one guy get away.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:31.840
Sure, you've been waiting all year to let
the beast out, and yes, your landlord probably

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:32.460
deserves it.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.920
But if they get away the first time, you've
got to chill.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.200
Relax there's always next year.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.140
Do: Leave the country

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.140
Sometimes the only way to win is not to play.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:46.480
So if you've got the means and motive, take
the opportunity, and get out of the country

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:47.180
on Purge night.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:51.940
Spend the night offshore in international
waters, or just move and say goodbye to the

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:55.800
US of A. You'll be home eventually how long
can this tradition really last?

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.900
Don't: Go Outside

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:01.860
The plots of Purge movies don't kick in until
the outside world intrudes.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:07.250
If you want to avoid that, then stay in and
plan ahead to avoid the need for a beer, pizza,

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:07.940
or ammo run.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:12.120
There's a reason why none of these movies
have focused too much on what goes down inside

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:16.099
most people's' homes during Purge night, and
that's because for most people, the Purge

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.140
is a downright cozy experience.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:22.820
It's people in fuzzy socks with AR-15s, eating
snacks and clearing out the DVR.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:27.040
For the most part, regular people don't really
go after each other during the Purge.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:28.240
It's live and let live.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:33.700
With four movies of documentary evidence to
go on, it's clear the Purge is for crazy people,

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.139
so let the crazy people have it.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.280
You don't have to go out there.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.080
Just stay inside and watch TV.

